  "content": {
    "id": "p33-q15-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "15",
    "prompt": "A couple decide to have offspring until they have at least one male and at least one female child. What is the expected number of children in this family?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": {
        "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
        "version": 1,
        "blocks": [
          {
            "id": "p33-q15-short-result",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "3 children.",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "p33-q15-short-method",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "After the first child, the expected wait for a child of the other sex is 2 more children.",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "worked": "Assume births are independent, with male and female equally likely. After the first child, let $W$ be the expected number of additional children until a child of the other sex is born. The next child ends the wait with probability $\\frac12$; otherwise the same wait starts again.\n$$\\begin{align*}W&=\\frac12\\times1+\\frac12(1+W)\\\\W&=1+\\frac12W\\\\\\frac12W&=1\\\\W&=2\\end{align*}$$\nIncluding the first child,\n$$\\begin{align*}E(N)&=1+W\\\\E(N)&=3.\\end{align*}$$\nThe expected family size is 3 children.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 55
  },
